Checkpoint an accepted Change Request revision.

The accepted candidate tree becomes one internal commit on the Story branch,
created under a compare-and-swap on the branch tip. The leaf remains integrating:
nothing is landed on trunk, and internal checkpoints only delimit later Task
diffs and make the work recoverable before the final Story squash.

A Change Request with repository_delta=empty creates no commit — its tree would
equal its parent's — and the leaf likewise remains integrating.

Only the tracked integration run bound to the accepted revision's producer role
and archetype may run this command. Reviewers, orchestrators, and other producer
archetypes are refused.

Usage:
  task-board worktree checkpoint <ELEMENT-ID> [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for checkpoint

Global Flags:
      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default ".task-board")
      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite
      --insecure                 Skip TLS certificate verification (for self-signed certs)
      --json                     Output in JSON format
      --no-update-check          Disable automatic update check
      --remote string            Remote board server URL (overrides TASK_BOARD_REMOTE)
      --remote-board string      Remote board ID (overrides TASK_BOARD_ID)

